    <programme start="20260705003000 +0800" stop="20260705010000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Yukon for Sale 第1季第8集 -Sarah and Sarah with James</title>
      <desc>Single Sarah is a Yukon newbie and has never bought a house before, so she enlists her skeptical friend, Sarah, to help her out.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705010000 +0800" stop="20260705020000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Facing Forces of Nature 第1季第1集 -Asteroids</title>
      <desc>Do we have a chance against a planet killer asteroid from space?</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705020000 +0800" stop="20260705023000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Andy and Ben Eat Australia 第3季第1集 -South Australia</title>
      <desc>In the first part of the episode, Andy explores sustainable kingfish farming in Spencer Gulf, South Australia, visiting Clean Seas sea farm and preparing fresh kingfish sashimi with the team. Moving to Kangaroo Island, he learns pickling techniques with Kate from Kangaroo Island Source, showcasing her products in a Carne Asada Taco. The episode continues with Andy exploring d&amp;apos;Arenberg&amp;apos;s multi-function building and &amp;apos;The Cube,&amp;apos; experiencing a Chef&amp;apos;s Table, and concludes at Wirra Wirra winery, where he cooks Yogurt Flatbread with Olive Oil and Dukka, enjoying it with the staff and their wines.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705023000 +0800" stop="20260705030000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Andy and Ben Eat Australia 第3季第2集 -Northern Territory</title>
      <desc>In Kakadu National Park, Andy joins Dewayne Webb foraging pandanus and cooking Seared Buffalo with Pandanus &amp;amp; Charred Herb Salsa over an open fire. He then heads to Darwin, assisting Zach Green at Elijah’s Kitchen, a food truck offering indigenous-inspired meals like Magpie Goose and Crocodile Laksa. Returning to Kakadu, Andy goes fishing with local Barramundi expert Rob Johnson and prepares Paperbark Leaf BBQ Barramundi with Sour Tamarind Sauce at Anbangbang Billabong, showcasing the region&amp;apos;s environment and produce.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705030000 +0800" stop="20260705040000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Bear&amp;apos;s Mission With Rob Brydon 第1季第2集 -Rob Brydon</title>
      <desc>Funny man Rob Brydon joins Bear Grylls for an adventure he won’t forget as he takes on a mission in the Mountains of Snowdonia.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705040000 +0800" stop="20260705043000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Brave Wilderness 第2季第3集 -Operation Rhino: White Rhino Dehorning &amp;amp; Black Rhino GPS Tech Implant!</title>
      <desc>Coyote dehorns a white rhino and implants a GPS tracker into a rare black rhino!</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705043000 +0800" stop="20260705050000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Brave Wilderness 第2季第4集 -Entering the Wolf Den &amp;amp; Wild Deer Carcass Feeding Frenzy!</title>
      <desc>Coyote meets rescued foxes, then feeds a deer carcass to a pack of powerful gray wolves!</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705050000 +0800" stop="20260705053000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Experience Australia 第1季第1集 -Central Australia</title>
      <desc>In this first episode, we showcase the best experiences on offer in Central Australia, also known as ‘The Red Centre.’ This ancient land is brimming with natural wonders and cultural significance. See Uluru at sunrise, experience life as a cattle farmer, learn about Australia’s rich indigenous history and walk the treacherous Larapinta Trail.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705053000 +0800" stop="20260705060000 +0800" channel="311">
      <title>Experience Australia 第1季第10集 -Southern Western Australia</title>
      <desc>From the towering Karri forests of Warren National Park to the ancient rock formations of The Pinnacles, Western Australia’s southern region is a treasure of natural wonders. In the final installment of Experience Australia, we highlight the best experiences for visitors to this magical region. Explore the pristine coastline and cuddly wildlife residents of Rottnest Island, immerse yourself in an indigenous cultural experience at Yanchep National Park, and embark on a thrilling sea voyage to encounter the elusive killer whale.</desc>
    </programme>
    <programme start="20260705060000 +0800" stop="20260705063000 +0800" channel="311">
